---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="About Ali Maghami"
	pubDate={new Date('September 01 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		I'm Ali Maghami, a software engineer and researcher interested in computer vision, robotics, and applied AI for industrial automation. I currently work at Hatch Ltd. in Ontario, Canada, where I help teams develop vision and AI solutions for manufacturing and mining applications.
	</p>

	<h2>Background</h2>
	<p>
		I completed my PhD in Mechanical Engineering at the University of Manitoba, where I focused on vision-guided robotics and machine learning. Before that, I worked at TetraGen Robotics on perception systems for automation, and I've also contributed to research at the National Research Council Canada.
	</p>

	<h2>What I Work On</h2>
	<p>
		My work involves computer vision, robotics, machine learning, calibration, and systems integration. I'm interested in taking research ideas and turning them into practical solutions that work in real manufacturing environments. Recent projects have included large-scale vision systems, deep learning for inspection, and robot calibration methods.
	</p>

	<h2>Skills & Interests</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Computer Vision: 2D/3D imaging, camera calibration, stereo vision</li>
		<li>Machine Learning: Deep learning, PyTorch, synthetic data, training workflows</li>
		<li>Robotics: Robot guidance, perception systems, collaborative robots</li>
		<li>Software: Python, C++, OpenCV, Open3D, cloud deployment</li>
		<li>Leadership: Team coordination, technical mentorship, project planning</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Education</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>PhD in Mechanical Engineering (University of Manitoba, 2023)</li>
		<li>MSc in Mechanical Engineering (Ferdowsi University of Mashhad, 2012)</li>
		<li>BSc in Mechanical Engineering (Ferdowsi University of Mashhad, 2010)</li>
		<li>PMP Certification (Project Management Professional)</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Publications & Patents</h2>
	<p>
		I've published research in peer-reviewed journals on topics like robot calibration, vision-guided drilling, and inspection automation. I also hold patents related to vision systems for industrial applications. You can find my recent publications in the blog section.
	</p>

	<h2>Beyond Work</h2>
	<p>
		I enjoy learning new technologies, exploring how AI and robotics can improve manufacturing processes, and collaborating with teams on technical challenges. I'm always interested in connecting with others working on similar problems.
	</p>
</Layout>
